  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the stereotype and the visual metaphor",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the meme's core message, which equates white people with fish and uses the visual of a naval gun firing as a metaphor for 'attacking' this ignorance. The user is implicitly positioned as someone who might be 'shooting down' or reacting to the stereotype, even though the meme itself does not contain explicit deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me'. The projection is onto the textual material ('fish swim in schools') and the visual material (naval gunner firing) which together form the stereotype and its aggressive dismissal.",
